WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.467 --> 00:00:09.321
The fox is a very clever animal.

2
00:00:09.322 --> 00:00:12.276
He can get whatever he needs.

3
00:00:12.277 --> 00:00:17.240
He can eat whatever he wants.

4
00:00:17.241 --> 00:00:21.384
Being clever all the time was not easy for the fox.

5
00:00:21.385 --> 00:00:23.475
It was a lot of hard work.

6
00:00:23.476 --> 00:00:26.658
So he really needed his rest.

7
00:00:26.659 --> 00:00:32.252
The fox took a nap every afternoon.

8
00:00:32.253 --> 00:00:36.555
One afternoon, the fox was awakened from his nap.

9
00:00:36.556 --> 00:00:38.321
It was a crow.

10
00:00:38.322 --> 00:00:43.625
She was carrying a big piece of cheese in her beak.

11
00:00:43.626 --> 00:00:46.923
The fox stared at the cheese.

12
00:00:46.924 --> 00:00:50.990
"Look at that cheese," he said to himself.

13
00:00:50.991 --> 00:00:54.554
"I'm sure it tastes delicious.

14
00:00:54.555 --> 00:00:59.933
I must have some of that cheese!"

15
00:00:59.934 --> 00:01:02.911
The fox thought and thought.

16
00:01:02.912 --> 00:01:05.907
Finally, he had an idea.

17
00:01:05.908 --> 00:01:11.781
The fox pretended to be asleep.

18
00:01:11.782 --> 00:01:14.236
The fox stretched his body.

19
00:01:14.237 --> 00:01:21.357
"Ahh," he yawned loudly.

20
00:01:21.358 --> 00:01:24.128
The fox looked up at the crow.

21
00:01:24.129 --> 00:01:28.188
Then he put his hand upon his heart.

22
00:01:28.189 --> 00:01:34.695
"Oh, hello. Am I still dreaming?" the fox asked aloud.

23
00:01:34.696 --> 00:01:41.611
"You are the most beautiful crow I have ever seen!"

24
00:01:41.612 --> 00:01:43.664
The crow was embarrassed.

25
00:01:43.665 --> 00:01:46.023
She did not know what to say.

26
00:01:46.024 --> 00:01:49.995
The fox continued, "Look at your feathers.

27
00:01:49.996 --> 00:01:53.777
They shine like the sun!"

28
00:01:53.778 --> 00:01:56.877
The crow spread her wings a little more.

29
00:01:56.878 --> 00:02:01.990
"Your eyes are bright like the moon," the fox admired.

30
00:02:01.991 --> 00:02:05.845
The crow opened her eyes wide.

31
00:02:05.846 --> 00:02:12.425
"Such a beautiful bird must have a beautiful voice."

32
00:02:12.426 --> 00:02:15.714
The fox slyly looked at the crow.

33
00:02:15.715 --> 00:02:20.364
"How I would love to hear a song from you!

34
00:02:20.365 --> 00:02:26.256
Then I will call you Queen of the Birds!"

35
00:02:26.257 --> 00:02:29.329
The crow held up her head high.

36
00:02:29.330 --> 00:02:34.155
She opened her mouth, and out came a loud caw.

37
00:02:34.156 --> 00:02:39.742
"Caw! Caw! Caw!" she cried.

38
00:02:39.743 --> 00:02:47.092
At the same time, out dropped the piece of cheese.

39
00:02:47.093 --> 00:02:52.124
The fox quickly jumped up and caught the cheese in his mouth.

40
00:02:52.125 --> 00:02:54.464
The crow stopped singing.

41
00:02:54.465 --> 00:02:59.610
"Oh, my cheese!" she cried out.

42
00:02:59.611 --> 00:03:03.427
But it was too late.

43
00:03:03.428 --> 00:03:06.223
The fox got what he wanted.

44
00:03:06.224 --> 00:03:13.820
"Your voice is good," the fox finally said, "but let me give you some advice.

45
00:03:13.821 --> 00:03:21.716
Don't trust those who flatter you!"
